From 1b459f1b411a578293ef22b2e2556b15994168eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:45:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] renderers/drm: Give a stereo theme the depth limits of its
 output

plymouth.stereo= entries take popped=PIXELS and sunk=PIXELS: how far in front
of the screen and behind it the splash may put things on that output, pixels of
an eye 1920 wide, the unit of the desktop's own limits (Stereo KWin's
PoppedLimit and SunkLimit built on the display). The script plugin gets
Window.GetStereoPoppedLimit () and Window.GetStereoSunkLimit (), so a theme
places its levels inside them. An entry without them gets the desktop's
defaults, 4 and 10, and the renderer says so once per output; a value that is
no limit (not a number, negative, over 1000) is said and the default stands.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
